<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/>;
    dc:modified '2012-06-27T12:15:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'DED'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'District Electoral Divisions'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A district electoral division (often abbreviated as DED) is a former name given to a low-level territorial division in Ireland, wherein the population are eligible to vote on a representative for a particular seat in local, regional, and national elections. Also known as electoral divisions. In the Republic of Ireland, DEDs are the smallest legally defined administrative areas in the state for which small area population statistics (SAPS) are published from the Census. There are a total of 3,440 electoral divisions within the Republic of Ireland.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A04::DistrictElectoralDivisions'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/>;
    dc:modified '2012-06-27T12:15:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'DED'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Division de distritos electorales'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A district electoral division (often abbreviated as DED) is a former name given to a low-level territorial division in Ireland, wherein the population are eligible to vote on a representative for a particular seat in local, regional, and national elections. Also known as electoral divisions. In the Republic of Ireland, DEDs are the smallest legally defined administrative areas in the state for which small area population statistics (SAPS) are published from the Census. There are a total of 3,440 electoral divisions within the Republic of Ireland.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A04::DistrictElectoralDivisions'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/>;
    dc:modified '2012-06-27T12:15:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'DED'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'District Electoral Divisions'@en ;
    skos:definition 'La división de distritos electorales (abreviada en ingles como DED) es el nombre anterior dado a las divisiones territoriales mas pequeñas en Irlanda, donde los habitantes pueden ejercer su derecho a voto tanto a nivel local, como regional, y nacionales. También conocido como división electoral. En la Republica de Irlanda, son el área legal más pequeña en cuanto a las áreas administrativas y de control estadístico de censo. Hay un total de 3440 divisiones electorales en la Republica de Irlanda.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A04::DistrictElectoralDivisions'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DistrictElectoralDivisions/>;
    dc:modified '2012-06-27T12:15:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'DED'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Division de distritos electorales'@en ;
    skos:definition 'La división de distritos electorales (abreviada en ingles como DED) es el nombre anterior dado a las divisiones territoriales mas pequeñas en Irlanda, donde los habitantes pueden ejercer su derecho a voto tanto a nivel local, como regional, y nacionales. También conocido como división electoral. En la Republica de Irlanda, son el área legal más pequeña en cuanto a las áreas administrativas y de control estadístico de censo. Hay un total de 3440 divisiones electorales en la Republica de Irlanda.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A04::DistrictElectoralDivisions'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DigitalTerrainModel/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DigitalTerrainModel/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/A04/current/DigitalTerrainModel/>;
    dc:modified '2012-06-27T12:15:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'DTM'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Digital Terrain Model'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A Digital Terrain Model (DTM) is a continuous representation of a ground surface landform that is commonly used to produce topographic maps. DTMs are created by integrating data obtained from a wide range of techniques including remote sensing and land surveying.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:A04::DigitalTerrainModel'^^xsd:string .
